{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1479891183,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MjQ2MDM2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1127#issuecomment-262460363"},"message":"Did you try with all the SSH fixes in #1037?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1479902926,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MjQ5NzA4NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1127#issuecomment-262497085"},"message":"On November 23, 2016 3:53:03 AM EST, Benjamin Poldrack notifications@github.com wrote:\n\n\u003e Did you try with all the SSH fixes in #1037?\n\u003e \n\u003e ## \n\u003e \n\u003e You are receiving this because you authored the thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub:\n\u003e https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1127#issuecomment-262460363\n\nAh, forgot that it was there and not yet finished/merged... Did you try it?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1479913024,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MjUzNjExNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1127#issuecomment-262536115"},"message":"Nope. Can't log into smaug recently and didn't figure out yet, what this is about.\nBut what I did try is to simulate it by installing datasets.datalad.org locally and then again from the local source via `localhost: ...`, so I have an SSH source. It behaves like you described in master, but with `rf-publish` branch it's somewhat different. It works nicely at the first level but then also starts asking for password for seemingly every subdataset at the second level.\nSo - conclusion: The issue is different but \"real\". ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485145003,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDM5NzMyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1127#issuecomment-274397327"},"message":"I think I got it.\n\nThis happened, whenever we `git annex init`-ed a fresh clone, which had to enable a datalad special remote. For some reason this led to an exception in `AnnexRepo.__del__` (`TypeError NoneType not callable`). I didn't figure out where this comes from, but worked around it by ignoring this kind of exception, since it is unlikely to cause some harm. However, this was not the actual issue. Instead the problem came from having two datalad processes. One for the actual datalad command, that calls `git annex init`, which in return creates a second datalad process to enable our special remote. Therefore we had two independent `SSHManager` instances, using the same connections. Ending the special remote process then led to \"clean up\" and close all connections used by `SSHManager`. Therefore the connections originally opened by the datalad command's `SSHManager` were closed and needed to be opened again.\nSee PR #1206\n\n@yarikoptic : Can you confirm this doesn't happen anymore?","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485402763,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTM3MjU1Nzg1"},"status":2}]}